, any program will compute a default x and y position. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"position attributes let this be changed two ways."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"font","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The font attribute group gathers together attributes for determining the font"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"within a credit or direction. They are based on the text styles for Cascading"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Style Sheets. The font-family is a comma-separated list of font names. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"font-style can be normal or italic. The font-size can be one of the CSS sizes or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a numeric point size. The font-weight can be normal or bold. The default is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"application-dependent, but is a text font vs. a music font."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"color","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The color attribute group indicates the color of an element."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"usesPlusMinus","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A Boolean value indicating whether plus and minus symbols should be used instead"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of sharp and flat symbols to display the degree alteration. "},{"code":"false","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" if not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"specified."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldegree\/alter-swift.struct\/init(value:position:font:color:usesplusminus:)"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Creates a new "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MXLDegree.Alter"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"init","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"value","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"position","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLPosition","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL11MXLPositionV"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"font","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLFont","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLFontV"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"color","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLColor","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"usesPlusMinus","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"},{"text":"?)","kind":"text"}],"roleHeading":"Initializer","title":"init(value:position:font:color:usesPlusMinus:)","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLDegreeV5AlterV5value8position4font5color13usesPlusMinusAESd_AA11MXLPositionVAA7MXLFontVAA8MXLColorVSgSbSgtcfc"},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLPosition":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"For most elements, any program will compute a default x and y position. The position attributes let this be"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"changed two ways."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlposition","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLPosition"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLPosition","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLPosition"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPosition","role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLColor":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The color type indicates the color of an element. Color may be represented as hexadecimal RGB triples, as in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"HTML, or as hexadecimal ARGB tuples, with the A indicating alpha of transparency. An alpha value of 00 is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"totally transparent; FF is totally opaque. If RGB is used, the A value is assumed to be FF."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlcolor","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLColor","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLColor","role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDegree":{"type":"topic","title":"MXLDegree","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDegree","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The degree type is used to add, alter, or subtract individual notes in the chord. The print-object attribute"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can be used to keep the degree from printing separately when it has already taken into account in the text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"attribute of the kind element. The degree-value and degree-type text attributes specify how the value and type"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of the degree should be displayed."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLDegree"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLDegree"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldegree"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDegree/Alter-swift.struct":{"type":"topic","title":"MXLDegree.Alter","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDegree\/Alter-swift.struct","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The degree-alter type represents the chromatic alteration for the current degree. If the degree-type value is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"alter or subtract, the degree-alter value is relative to the degree already in the chord based on its kind"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"element. If the degree-type value is add, the degree-alter is relative to a dominant chord (major and perfect"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"intervals except for a minor seventh). The plus-minus attribute is used to indicate if plus and minus symbols"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"should be used instead of sharp and flat symbols to display the degree alteration. It is no if not specified."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Alter","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Alter","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldegree\/alter-swift.struct"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLFont":{"type":"topic","title":"MXLFont","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLFont","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The font attribute group gathers together attributes for determining the font within a credit or direction."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"They are based on the text styles for Cascading Style Sheets. The font-family is a comma-separated list of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"font names. The font-style can be normal or italic. The font-size can be one of the CSS sizes or a numeric"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"point size. The font-weight can be normal or bold. The default is application-dependent, but is a text font"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vs. a music font."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLFont"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLFont"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlfont"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDegree/Alter-swift.struct/init(value:position:font:color:usesPlusMinus:)":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"value","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"position","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLPosition","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL11MXLPositionV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"font","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLFont","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLFontV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"color","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLColor","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"usesPlusMinus","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?)","kind":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDegree\/Alter-swift.struct\/init(value:position:font:color:usesPlusMinus:)","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Creates a new "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MXLDegree.Alter"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"title":"init(value:position:font:color:usesPlusMinus:)","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldegree\/alter-swift.struct\/init(value:position:font:color:usesplusminus:)"}}}